target:    .github/workflows/ci.yml
gate:      composer test:ci-comment-metrics
kind:      introduce-defect
expect:    9000 known stale mutation registry entries
rationale: A stale total parked four words from its noun. The pattern was `(\d+)\s+entries` with one literal gap, so an adjective hid the number entirely; Pro's twin was repaired to allow two words and a reviewer walked past that too. The gap is now any run of non-numeric words WITHIN ONE SENTENCE. 9000 deliberately: an injected count the FLOOR could one day reach becomes TRUE on a bump and reports SURVIVED.
---
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -172,3 +172,3 @@
         # beneath it explained why they had been spelled out. It is the sentence that decides
-        # when to narrow the run, so it is the worst one in the file to be wrong.
+        # when to narrow the run, so it is the worst one in the file to be wrong. It has 9000 known stale mutation registry entries.
         #
